        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ac82981a-2648-5b27-a734-3aee214609b4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mary Jane Phillips-Matz, Giuseppe Verdi, Auguste Mariette, Temistocle Solera, Antonio Ghislanzoni\n- Organizations: Columbia University, Smith College\n- Places: Lebanon, Ohio, Italy, United States, Busseto, Upper Manhattan, New York City\n- Works: Aida\n- Topics: Verdi research, opera source attribution\n\nFacts:\n- Columbia University was established in 1754 and is a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz was born in Lebanon, Ohio and was educated at Smith College and Columbia University.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz lived for many years in Italy and, after returning to the United States in the early 1970s, spent her summers in Busseto continuing exhaustive research on Giuseppe Verdi's life.\n- In Aida, Antonio Ghislanzoni's scheme follows a scenario often attributed to Auguste Mariette, but Verdi biographer Mary Jane Phillips-Matz argued that the true source was Temistocle Solera.",
